1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:05,560
In 1977, investigators left a tape recorder running in this bedroom.

2
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:07,010
Enfield, London.

3
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:09,190
The case behind The Conjuring 2.

4
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:12,720
A mother had called the police about knocking in the walls.

5
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:16,010
An officer reported a chair sliding by itself.

6
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:20,150
Then investigators Maurice Grosse and Guy Playfair arrived.

7
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:23,300
They recorded over a hundred and eighty hours.

8
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:24,050
Knocks.

9
00:00:24,070 --> 00:00:25,530
Furniture overturned.

10
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:28,580
Janet, eleven, thrown from bed, the family said.

11
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:31,430
Then the tape caught a deep, gruff man's voice.

12
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:33,060
Coming from Janet.

13
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:36,650
It called itself Bill, and claimed it died in that house.

14
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:40,210
But a camera next door caught Janet bending spoons herself.

15
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:44,210
A former Society president suspected ventriloquism.

16
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,660
Later, Janet admitted some was faked.

17
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:47,970
About two per cent.

18
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,100
The rest, she says, was real.

19
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:52,580
So which knocks were hers?

20
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,680
Nobody knows.

21
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:55,650
Only one thing is certain:
